      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/priddy-tx",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first homes in Priddy appeared in the early 1880s, built mainly by German settlers who brought their traditions to the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/priddy-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Priddy’s first post office opened in 1892, making the town an early communication hub for northeast Mills County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/priddy-tx",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The local climate is humid subtropical, with warm temperatures and fairly even rainfall throughout the year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
